1. What you may do without an agreement

   You may read the Enterprise Software, copy it and change it, but only to
   develop and test it, or to develop and test changes you plan to
   contribute back to Slatebox LLC. You may run it for those purposes on
   your own computers and test systems.

   You may also copy, install and run the Enterprise Software, unchanged or
   changed, in production, for real users and with real data, as part of any
   install of Slatebox: Slatebox Cloud, or Slatebox installed on your own or
   anyone else's servers. This use is free of charge and needs no license
   key.

2. What needs an agreement

   Any other use needs a written agreement with Slatebox LLC. "Other use"
   includes, without limit:

   a. running the Enterprise Software, or a changed version of it, apart
      from Slatebox, or as part of a product other than Slatebox;
   b. offering it, or a service built on it, to anyone else, hosted or not,
      except as part of an install of Slatebox that section 1 allows;
   c. selling, sublicensing, renting or distributing it, or a changed
      version of it, on its own or as part of another product. This does
      not limit passing on a copy of Slatebox, with this license kept in
      it, for someone to run under section 1;
   d. offering Slatebox with the Enterprise Software in it to others as a
      paid hosted service. Running Slatebox for your own organization, or
      hosting it for others at no charge, needs no agreement.

   Slatebox LLC runs the Enterprise Software as part of Slatebox Cloud. Using
   Slatebox Cloud under its terms of service is the agreement that covers
   people who use these features there.

